# Machine-local paths for hook commands in settings.json.
#
# import.sh writes this file during step 12, and write-paths-local.sh in this
# directory does it on demand — both derive the checkout rather than guessing a
# layout. This example is the documented shape, for reading or for filling in by
# hand. Do not commit the filled-in copy:
# ~/.claude is not a repo, and export.sh reads only settings.json, so the value
# stays local by construction.
#
# Hook commands source this file and refuse to run — exit 2, blocking the tool
# call — when a path it should define is missing. That is deliberate: the hooks
# it points at are safety guards, and a guard that silently is not there is
# worse than one that fails loudly.

# Checkout of the agents-shared repo, which holds hooks/ and claude/rules/.
# Whatever this machine actually uses, e.g. $HOME/dev/agents-shared or
# $HOME/src/agents-shared or $HOME/work/tools/agents-shared.
AGENTS_SHARED_DIR="$HOME/path/to/agents-shared"
